Description: take-your-time keep-awake tray indicator
 slow-coffee is a small system-tray coffee cup that stops your screen blanking
 and your session going idle. It is on by default - the cup boots full - because
 the point is to stay awake until you say otherwise.
 .
 Idle is inhibited over D-Bus, preferring the running session daemon
 (org.gnome.SessionManager, then org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver) and falling back
 to systemd-inhibit. Idle-only by default, so closing the lid still suspends.
